  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday) \nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nSunday and Monday the stagnant pattern will continue. High \ntemperatures will stay hot and near normal both days. Humidity will \nremain low enough to keep heat indices below Heat Advisory criteria, \nhowever a few spots in the Coastal Plains could briefly reach \ncriteria each afternoon. A few showers or thunderstorms could move \nover the Coastal Plains each afternoon. As the ridge shifts back \ntoward the southeast, rain chances will come to an end Tuesday. \nTemperatures will creep up a bit into the middle of next week. The \nhigher temperatures combined with the humidity may produce Heat \nAdvisory criteria across the area south of I-10 and east of I-37.",
